# Test artifacts
*.png
*.mp4

# …except the shipped example storyboards' media. Their stills and clips are
# curated assets built by scripts/build-example-storyboards.mjs and served as
# `package://` URIs; the blanket *.mp4 above swallowed every one of them.
!nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/storyboards/**

# …and the Game flow's style tiles and template cards, drawn by
# scripts/make-game-style-tiles.mjs and served as `package://` URIs.
!nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/styles/**
!nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/templates/**

# Shipped example games include PNG sprites, backgrounds, and color grades.
!nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/games/**/*.png

# …and the example timelines' rendered videos and posters, written by
# scripts/render-example-timeline.mjs and served as `package://` URIs.
!nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/timelines/**
%Y-%m-%d-%H-%M-%S.txt
\[object\ Object\]/

# File-system node test outputs
bin.dat
dst.txt
ex.txt
f.txt
info.txt
log.txt
new.txt
notes/
sized.txt
src.txt
sub/
test.txt
top/
# Package media lives on media.nodetool.ai, listed in
# nodetool/assets/nodetool-base.media.json. `node scripts/package-media.mjs pull`
# fills these folders and `push` uploads new files. Text files stay in git.
# Storyboard films play from media.nodetool.ai/showcase and never ship.
nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/storyboards/*/*.mp4
nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/games/**/*.jpg
nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/games/**/*.jpeg
nodetool/assets/nodetool-base/games/**/*.png
